            "question": "Do solar attic fans actually work?",
            "answer": "<p>They do. Attics trap radiant heat all summer, which drives cooling costs up and shortens shingle life. A solar attic fan runs off its own panel — no added power bill — and continuously pulls that hot air out.</p>"
